Here's how to implement a dark mode toggle using only CSS with a checkbox hack:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Dark Mode Toggle</title>
    <style>
        /* Default light theme */
        :root {
            --bg: #ffffff;
            --text: #222222;
            --primary: #0066cc;
            --card: #f0f0f0;
        }

        body {
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            transition: background 0.3s, color 0.3s;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 40px;
            min-height: 100vh;
        }

        /* Hide the checkbox */
        #darkmode-toggle {
            display: none;
        }

        /* When checkbox is checked, override variables to dark theme */
        #darkmode-toggle:checked ~ .page {
            --bg: #1a1a2e;
            --text: #e0e0e0;
            --primary: #8ab4f8;
            --card: #16213e;
        }

        /* Label styled as toggle switch */
        .toggle-label {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            background: var(--primary);
            color: white;
            border-radius: 20px;
            cursor: pointer;
            user-select: none;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .page {
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            transition: background 0.3s, color 0.3s;
        }

        .card {
            background: var(--card);
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            margin: 10px 0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <input type="checkbox" id="darkmode-toggle">
    <div class="page">
        <label for="darkmode-toggle" class="toggle-label">Toggle Dark Mode</label>
        <h1>Dark Mode Demo</h1>
        <p>Toggle the switch above to change between light and dark mode using only CSS.</p>
        <div class="card">
            <h3>How it works</h3>
            <p>This uses the checkbox hack with CSS custom properties (variables). When the checkbox is checked, the CSS :checked pseudo-class changes the --bg, --text, and --primary variables to dark mode values.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

The key technique uses:
- CSS custom properties (variables) for colors in `:root`
- A hidden checkbox `#darkmode-toggle`
- The `:checked` pseudo-class to detect when dark mode is selected
- The general sibling combinator `~` to apply dark mode variables to the `.page` container when the checkbox is checked
- `transition: background 0.3s, color 0.3s` for smooth transitions
